You're on the right track!  Adding a Gaussian filter before Sobel is a common and effective technique to enhance edge detection by reducing noise. Here's the modified MATLAB code incorporating this improvement along with a detailed explanation:

```matlab
input_image = imread('image.jpg'); 
gray_image = rgb2gray(input_image);

% 1. Gaussian Smoothing (Noise Reduction)
sigma = 1.5;  % Adjust sigma for desired blur level (higher = more smoothing)
gaussian_filter = fspecial('gaussian', [5 5], sigma); % Create Gaussian kernel
smoothed_image = imfilter(gray_image, gaussian_filter, 'replicate'); % Apply filtering

